{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZpW5VeWkHTdeow7jigQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! The existing tests pass. Now I have enough understanding of the repository structure and conventions. Let me summarize my analysis:\n\n**Requirement, restated:**\nAdd a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that transitions a shipment from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED`, handles retries idempotently, rejects cancelled shipments with 409, and rejects unknown shipments with 404.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:9-27` - Shipment model with ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentController.kt:1-56` - REST controller (POST create, GET by id, GET list; no confirm endpoint yet)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:1-27` - In-memory repository (save, findById, existsById, findAll)\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:1-30` - ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409)\n- `ApiError.kt:1-37` - Error envelope and ErrorCode enum\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:1-29` - Central exception handler\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt:1-84` - Existing shipment tests (all pass)\n\n**Conventions:**\n1. Endpoints throw ApiException subclasses which GlobalExceptionHandler converts to ApiError envelopes\n2. 404 errors → ResourceNotFoundException\n3. 409 errors → ConflictException\n4. All error codes must be added to ErrorCode enum\n5. POST creation returns HttpStatus.CREATED\n6. Tests use MockMvc and jsonPath to verify status and error responses\n7. @BeforeEach resets repository for test isolation\n\n**Affected files (required changes):**\n1. `ApiError.kt` - Add SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` - Add POST confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Add tests for confirm operation\n\n**Risks:**\n- Idempotency: confirming already CONFIRMED must succeed without error\n- State validation: only CREATED → CONFIRMED allowed; CANCELLED must reject\n- Unknown shipment must return 404, not error\n\n**Open questions:** None.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes (file by file):**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` error code to the ErrorCode enum. This code is used when attempting to confirm a shipment that is already CANCELLED.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new method `confirm` with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by id; if not found, throws ResourceNotFoundException\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent)\n   - If status is CREATED, update it to CONFIRMED\n   - Always save and return the shipment with 200 OK status\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test methods:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment and transitions to CONFIRMED` - verifies status changes\n   - `retrying confirm on CONFIRMED shipment succeeds idempotently` - verifies no error on retry\n   - `rejects confirm on CANCELLED shipment with 409` - verifies error code SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n   - `rejects confirm on unknown shipment with 404` - verifies error code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- *Adding a service layer* - Not needed; repository is simple and controller logic is minimal. This would add unnecessary complexity.\n- *Using a generic error code like VALIDATION_FAILED* - Rejected; the error is not a validation failure but a state conflict. SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE is more semantic.\n- *Returning 201 Created instead of 200 OK* - Rejected; confirm is an action on an existing resource, not creation. 200 is appropriate.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Case 1: Confirm CREATED shipment*\n1. Request: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm`\n2. Controller retrieves shipment (found, status = CREATED)\n3. No state conflict, not already CONFIRMED\n4. Create new Shipment with status = CONFIRMED\n5. Repository.save() persists it\n6. Response: 200 OK with updated Shipment JSON\n\n*Case 2: Confirm already CONFIRMED shipment (retry)*\n1. Request: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm`\n2. Controller retrieves shipment (found, status = CONFIRMED)\n3. No state conflict (condition is only for CANCELLED)\n4. Already confirmed: no state change needed\n5. Repository.save() with same Shipment (idempotent)\n6. Response: 200 OK with Shipment JSON (unchanged)\n\n*Case 3: Confirm CANCELLED shipment*\n1. Request: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm`\n2. Controller retrieves shipment (found, status = CANCELLED)\n3. State conflict: throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, message)\n4. GlobalExceptionHandler catches it\n5. Response: 409 Conflict with ApiError { code: SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, message: \"...\" }\n\n*Case 4: Confirm unknown shipment*\n1. Request: `POST /shipments/unknown/confirm`\n2. Controller tries to retrieve shipment (not found)\n3. Throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message)\n4. GlobalExceptionHandler catches it\n5. Response: 404 Not Found with ApiError { code: SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message: \"...\" }\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. `confirms a CREATED shipment` - Creates shipment, confirms it, asserts status changed to CONFIRMED and response is 200 OK\n2. `retry confirm on CONFIRMED` - Creates and confirms shipment, confirms again, asserts 200 OK and status unchanged\n3. `reject confirm on CANCELLED` - Directly saves CANCELLED shipment in repo, confirms it, asserts 409 Conflict with error code\n4. `reject confirm on unknown` - Confirms non-existent shipment, asserts 404 Not Found with error code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2391,"cache_read_input_tokens":21692,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2391},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"155b8b87-65ec-41ac-b1b0-010e3e0916ed","uuid":"54ad7ad5-5292-413c-a890-afddaff84808","timestamp":"2026-09-30T14:57:41.721Z","request_id":"req_011CfZpW56LanFDqCo4wU3M9"}
