{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZpchKbMuEunKxXLGSoX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me verify that all acceptance criteria are met by reviewing the implementation:\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. **Existing build passes** ✓\n   - `./mvnw test` completed successfully with BUILD SUCCESS\n\n2. **Existing tests pass** ✓\n   - All 13 original tests still pass (4 order + 1 app + 5 shipment + 3 customer)\n   - 4 new shipment tests added and all pass (9 shipment tests total)\n\n3. **POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm confirms a created shipment and persists it** ✓\n   - Test: `confirms a CREATED shipment and transitions to CONFIRMED` \n   - Endpoint: `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` in ShipmentController:57-78\n   - Implementation: Creates new Shipment with status CONFIRMED via `repository.save()`\n\n4. **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** ✓\n   - ResourceNotFoundException for unknown shipment (404) → SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n   - ConflictException for CANCELLED shipment (409) → SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n   - Both use the standard ApiError envelope via GlobalExceptionHandler\n\n5. **A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused** ✓\n   - Test: `retrying confirm on CONFIRMED shipment succeeds idempotently` — retrying confirm returns 200 OK with no error\n   - Test: `rejects confirm on CANCELLED shipment with 409` — returns 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - Test: `rejects confirm on unknown shipment with 404` — returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n6. **No new Maven dependency appears** ✓\n   - pom.xml unchanged, all existing dependencies used\n\n7. **No unrelated production file changes** ✓\n   - Only modified:\n     - `ApiError.kt` — added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code (necessary)\n     - `ShipmentController.kt` — added confirm endpoint and updated javadoc (necessary)\n     - `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — added 4 new tests (necessary)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Added `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to ErrorCode enum. Necessary because confirming a CANCELLED shipment must return a distinct error code for clients to differentiate from other errors.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added `confirm()` method with proper state transitions:\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if shipment doesn't exist (404)\n   - Throws ConflictException if shipment is CANCELLED (409)\n   - Returns unchanged shipment if already CONFIRMED (idempotent)\n   - Transitions CREATED → CONFIRMED and persists via repository\n   - Updated javadoc to reflect new feature\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 4 comprehensive tests:\n   - Confirms CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Idempotent retry on CONFIRMED succeeds\n   - Rejects CANCELLED with correct error code\n   - Rejects unknown shipment with correct error code\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All code is complete, no stubs or TODOs remain.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Add a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that transitions a shipment from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED`, handles retries idempotently, rejects cancelled shipments with 409, and rejects unknown shipments with 404.\n\nChanged:\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt` — Added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code for state conflict errors\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` — Added confirm endpoint with state validation and idempotent logic\n- `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Added 4 tests for confirm endpoint\n\nTests:\n- `confirms a CREATED shipment and transitions to CONFIRMED` — Verifies status changes from CREATED to CONFIRMED and returns 200 OK\n- `retrying confirm on CONFIRMED shipment succeeds idempotently` — Verifies